.TH ARENA:MEMORY:MONITOR 1 "June 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
arena:memory:monitor \- Monitor active MemoryArena worker allocations and trigger instantaneous zero-overhead resets.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBphp spp.php arena:memory:monitor\fR [\fB\-\-arena=\fI<name>\fR] [\fB\-\-capacity=\fI<MB>\fR] [\fB\-\-iterations=\fI<N>\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBarena:memory:monitor\fR command introduces high-performance, zero-allocation memory arena mechanics to long-running PHP CLI background daemons. Instead of relying on traditional PHP garbage collection—which causes periodic execution pauses and gradual memory fragmentation over months of continuous uptime—daemons pre-allocate contiguous memory arenas. Workers allocate objects within the arena during a job and instantly reset the arena offset pointer to zero upon completion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-arena=\fI<name>\fR
Name of the MemoryArena instance to initialize and monitor. Defaults to \fIspp_cqrs_worker_arena\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity=\fI<MB>\fR
Total contiguous memory capacity in megabytes to pre-allocate for the arena pool. Defaults to \fI64\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-iterations=\fI<N>\fR
Number of simulated worker job cycles to execute and reset. Defaults to \fI3\fR.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
1. \fBStrict SAPI Guarding\fR: Validates secure CLI execution via \fIisCLIOnly(): bool\fR.
.PP
2. \fBArena Pre-Allocation\fR: Reserves a contiguous memory block in user space corresponding to the requested capacity in megabytes.
.PP
3. \fBOffset Tracking\fR: Allocates worker objects (\fIpayload_json\fR, \fIentity_snapshot\fR, \fIw3c_trace_spans\fR) by advancing an internal byte offset pointer, completely bypassing traditional Zend engine heap allocation overhead.
.PP
4. \fBPointer Resets\fR: Upon worker job completion, instantaneously resets the allocation offset pointer back to zero. This effectively wipes all temporary job objects from memory in \fIO(1)\fR time without triggering a single garbage collection cycle.
